Certainly, any machine handling of the semantics of lojban texts would 
deploy many such rewrite rules to simplify and canonicalize the grammar.
There are so many alternate ways to express the same thing, and you don't 
want to have to handle them all separately.

I think there is some value in starting lojban lessons with the simplest, 
most useful, most universal words the language provides.
Knowing the equivalences would help a lot in identifying what is 
indispensible and what is mere syntactic sugar.

mihe bremenli

